# Frontend editor rules

## Stack & style
- React + TypeScript **strict**. No `any` — use `unknown` + narrowing. Named exports.
- Small, focused components; early returns; meaningful names; no magic numbers/strings.
- State changes to the timeline go through `editor-core` (typed ops + patch engine) — UI never mutates the project shape directly.

## Preview engine (HARD RULE, PRD §9.2)
- The UI preview uses **HTML `<video>`, canvas/WebGL overlays, and proxy/low-res media**.
- ❌ Never call MoviePy or the Python render engine for the real-time scrub/playback preview. Render (preview render & export) is a Python engine job invoked over IPC.

## Review UX (PRD §3.2)
- Every AI edit must be shown as a reviewable diff: **what changed, why, before/after preview, timeline diff, undo**. Apply / Edit prompt / Preview / Reject controls.

## Accessibility
- Keyboard-operable timeline and panels; visible focus states; ARIA roles/labels on custom controls; sufficient color contrast.
- Add accessibility tests alongside component/visual tests.

## Testing
- Component tests, integration tests, visual regression, accessibility tests (see `testing.mdc`).
- Critical flows are covered by Playwright e2e in `tests/e2e`.

## Plan & docs
- Update `plan/PLAN.md` and `docs/` (guide + CHANGELOG for user-facing changes) per `AGENTS.md`.
